PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,4},{2},{3,5}}

The 52 Genji incense patterns correspond one-to-one with the Bell number B_5=52 partitions of the 5-element set {1,2,3,4,5}. Chapters 2-53 are therefore an enumeration of those partitions. The canonical enumeration used here is the lexicographic order on restricted-growth strings (RGS) a=(a_2,a_3,a_4,a_5) where element i is placed in block a_i and each new label is the smallest non-negative integer not yet forbidden.

Under this ordering the given example for chapter 20 is the partition whose RGS is (1,0,0,2), which occupies position 18. Consequently chapter 39 occupies position 38. Counting shows that the first 15 strings begin with a_2=0 and the next 23 strings begin with a_2=1; the 23rd of those strings is (1,2,0,2). The blocks encoded by this RGS are exactly {1,4}, {2} and {3,5}, giving the required partition written in the canonical “blocks ordered by minimal element” form.

